{"id":"u-db72568b-91c7-4413-b0ff-35839d68df93","src":"community","title":"SBL-Lite Modern Bodybuilding Program","author":"Xander","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/xn0qI8-ul-ppl","desc":"Science Based Lifting can be fun -- but we don't really have evidence of somebody who has built a great physique on nothing but SBL.\n\nULPPL Has been ranked among one of the best splits by most modern builders. Where it trades off the 3.5x frequency of FBEOD, it gains in volume accumulation with a 2x frequency. Volume remains to be one of the only proven levers to force muscle growth. Frequency is only a different way to accumulate volume.\n\nAlso, compared to FBEOD, we can be in and out of the gym in ~45m-1h. And, for some people like me, I would prefer to go to the gym more often with shorter sessions than less often with longer sessions. If you are the opposite, this program might not be for you.\n\n1 RIR on compound movements is ideal, 0 RIR on isolation is great. Absolute failure should probably be avoided most of the time.\n\nRun the entire 8 weeks before changing exercises, rep ranges, or programs. The first few weeks will be neural adaptations; you will not gain muscle effectively if you switch out exercises too frequently.\n\nRun it, or don't, I don't really care. But I cooked up this heater program using some of the latest exercise data & modern bodybuilding consensus and wanted to share it.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-17T23:35:01.532Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper","Lower","Push","Pull","Legs"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Smith 30° Incline Bench","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Kelso Shrug (Chest Supported)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bayesian Curl","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Tricep Extension (Cable